Usage: printf FORMAT [ARGUMENT]...

Format and print data.

Print ARGUMENT(s) according to FORMAT.

Supported format specifiers:
  %%      Literal '%'
  %c      Character
  %s      String
  %d, %i  Integer
  %u      Unsigned integer
  %x, %X  Hexadecimal (lowercase/uppercase)
  %o      Octal
  %f      Floating point
  %e, %E  Scientific notation
  %g, %G  %f or %e depending on value
  %b      Interpret backslash escapes (like echo -e)


OPTIONS:
  -v ARG         assign the output to shell variable VAR
                 format and print data
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
